The '''Lancaster Brewing Company''' is an American brewery, restaurant and distillery  business located in [[Lancaster, Pennsylvania]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=BREWERY |url=https://www.lancasterbrewing.com/dine/lbc-brewery/ |access-date=2023-05-12 |website=Lancaster Brewing Co |language=en-US}}</ref> 

==History==
Founded in 1995, the brewery and the restaurant are located in the [[Edward McGovern Tobacco Warehouse]], which was listed on the [[National Register of Historic Places]] in 1990.<ref name="nris">{{NRISref|version=2010a}}</ref> In 2024, Lancaster Craft Spirits, a whiskey distillery was added to the business.  

The brewery has produced more than two hundred different beers since 1995.<ref>{{Cite web |title=our beer |url=https://www.lancasterbrewing.com/home/our-beer/ |access-date=2023-05-12 |website=Lancaster Brewing Co |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2013-09-20 |title=Lancaster Brewing Company Celebrates Oktoberfest |url=https://www.brewbound.com/news/lancaster-brewing-company-celebrates-oktoberfest |access-date=2024-03-15 |website=Brewbound |language=en-US}}</ref> Its products are sold throughout the [[Mid-Atlantic (United States)|Mid-Atlantic region]], with distribution in [[Pennsylvania]], [[New Jersey]], [[New York (state)|New York]], [[Washington, D.C.]], [[Delaware]], [[Maryland]] and [[Virginia]].

The grain to glass distillery produces American single malt whiskey, bourbon, hop infused gin, rum and vodka.

